{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'set +e\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" check >\"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stdout.txt\" 2>\"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stderr.txt\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON $STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER check\" >\"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.command.txt\"\nprintf '\"'check exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$?\"\npython3 - <<'\"'PY' >\\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-template-inspect.stdout.txt\"\nimport json,os\np=os.path.join(os.environ['\"'STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'],'response.json'); d=json.load(open(p)); print('top-level',list(d)); print('object',d.get('object')); print('assessor',d.get('assessor')); print('scope',d.get('scope'))\nPY\nprintf '%s\\\\n' 'python3 inspect response.json object metadata' >\\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-template-inspect.command.txt\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- check ---'; cat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stdout.txt\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stderr.txt\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-template-inspect.stdout.txt\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- REPORT LINE REFERENCES ---'; nl -ba \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/REPORT.md\" | sed -n '\"'1,130p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- ANALYSIS LINE REFERENCES ---'; nl -ba \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analyze.py\" | sed -n '\"'1,190p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'set +e\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" check >\"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stdout.txt\" 2>\"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stderr.txt\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON $STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER check\" >\"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.command.txt\"\nprintf '\"'check exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$?\"\npython3 - <<'\"'PY' >\\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-template-inspect.stdout.txt\"\nimport json,os\np=os.path.join(os.environ['\"'STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'],'response.json'); d=json.load(open(p)); print('top-level',list(d)); print('object',d.get('object')); print('assessor',d.get('assessor')); print('scope',d.get('scope'))\nPY\nprintf '%s\\\\n' 'python3 inspect response.json object metadata' >\\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-template-inspect.command.txt\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- check ---'; cat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stdout.txt\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/00-check.stderr.txt\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-template-inspect.stdout.txt\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- REPORT LINE REFERENCES ---'; nl -ba \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/REPORT.md\" | sed -n '\"'1,130p'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- ANALYSIS LINE REFERENCES ---'; nl -ba \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analyze.py\" | sed -n '\"'1,190p'\"","aggregated_output":"check exit=0\n--- check ---\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"source_commit\": \"9852d8360f9519d21d11099b45f5deb8ba80cb28\",\n  \"environment_commit\": \"3552d5003a2485b6405805236d5c54e7ed42f097\",\n  \"sha256\": {\n    \"pixi.toml\": \"131fc78549d9fe54a3e6c055e59ef753b1794df77507777b21c9529a611e7b89\",\n    \"pixi.lock\": \"f8fff1394fbeaa2ab1c4993fceb0dd6463fe0c08c81fcda397f3e752a72c4249\"\n  },\n  \"environment_repository\": \"https://github.com/leej3/stamped-ai-research-next.git\"\n}\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\ntop-level ['checklist_version', 'responses', 'schema_version', 'principles_version', 'checklist_source', 'extra_items', 'object', 'assessor', 'scope']\nobject {'url': None, 'commit': None, 'captured_at': None, 'kind': None}\nassessor {'skill': None, 'version': None, 'harness': None, 'model': None, 'date': None, 'dependencies': []}\nscope None\n--- REPORT LINE REFERENCES ---\n     1\t# Potential gains and vmPFC activity\n     2\t\n     3\t## Question and conclusion\n     4\t\n     5\tIn the 54-person NARPS equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not** support a positive gain association in vmPFC under whole-brain family-wise error (FWE) correction. In a bilateral medial orbitofrontal anatomical proxy for vmPFC, the mean participant effect was −0.008 supplied units (95% t interval −0.035 to 0.019); no voxel in that proxy survived whole-brain correction. This is absence of evidence for the predicted positive effect in these maps, not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero.\n     6\t\n     7\tThe whole-brain test did identify 23 positive FWE-significant voxels in three small posterior-inferior foci (peak t=6.62 at MNI [−26, −102, −3.6]; two other peaks are listed in `results/fwe_clusters.tsv`). These do not overlap the vmPFC proxy. They lie near the posterior-inferior edge of the analyzed brain; one peak is outside AAL3-labeled tissue. I therefore do not interpret them as evidence about gain coding or as a vmPFC finding.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Group model and inference\n    10\t\n    11\tI tested whether the unweighted mean of the 54 participant gain-effect estimates was greater than zero at each voxel. The maps are participant contrast parameter estimates, not t/z statistics. Because participant variance maps were not supplied, I used an unweighted one-sample group t statistic rather than precision-weighted second-level inference. A one-sided sign-flip randomization test (5,000 random sign patterns; fixed seed 20261016) evaluated the positive-direction hypothesis. For each randomization, I recorded the maximum t over the analysis mask; voxel p-values are adjusted against that maximum distribution, controlling whole-brain voxelwise FWE at 0.05. The 95th percentile maximum-t threshold was 5.39. Sign flipping assumes independent participants and a symmetric null distribution of participant effects. The original NARPS instructions posed a positive, region-specific hypothesis and required support decisions from whole-brain-corrected analyses; this analysis keeps that whole-brain correction rather than treating an uncorrected ROI result as support ([NARPS analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf); [permutation inference background](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6871862/)).\n    12\t\n    13\tThe analysis mask intersected an MNI152 standard brain mask with voxels nonzero in at least 49 of 54 maps and finite in every map (192,339 voxels). The vmPFC anatomical proxy was the bilateral `Frontal_Med_Orb` parcel in AAL3v2, mapped to the input grid using nearest-neighbor resampling. This is an explicit reproducible anatomical proxy, not a claim that one atlas parcel exhaustively defines functional vmPFC ([AAL3 atlas paper](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31521825/)). The ROI summary is descriptive; it does not replace or relax whole-brain correction.\n    14\t\n    15\t## Data checks and limitations\n    16\t\n    17\tAll 54 supplied maps matched the equal-indifference participant IDs, shared the same MNI grid, loaded with finite data, and passed the SHA256 values in the supplied manifest. No participant was excluded. The task’s potential-gain range was twice its potential-loss range, as described in the supplied methods. However, the upstream gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution, so these coefficients are not change per currency unit. The estimates are conditional on the upstream choice to model gain separately from loss and on its other fixed first-level terms. This group analysis cannot revisit those modeling decisions.\n    18\t\n    19\tThe lack of participant variance maps prevents a precision-weighted mixed-effects analysis and limits uncertainty modeling to variation across the supplied participant estimates. The permutation result relies on sign-flip symmetry. AAL3 medial orbitofrontal cortex is an imperfect vmPFC proxy, and the maps’ MNI152NLin2009cAsym space and the standard mask/atlas are not identical templates. The interval around the proxy mean includes zero and is not an equivalence interval: modest positive or spatially heterogeneous effects remain possible. A non-significant whole-brain-corrected result therefore means this group analysis did not establish a positive vmPFC effect at the chosen error rate; it does not show that increasing gains have no neural correlate. More broadly, the parametric map association does not establish that potential gain causally produces a response.\n    20\t\n    21\t## Figures\n    22\t\n    23\t**Figure 1.** Participant-average effect within bilateral medial orbitofrontal vmPFC proxy. Each dot is one participant; the diamond and interval show the mean and descriptive 95% t interval across participants.\n    24\t\n    25\t![Participant effects in vmPFC proxy](results/vmPFC_proxy_effects.png)\n    26\t\n    27\t**Figure 2.** Positive t statistics exceeding the 95th percentile of the whole-brain maximum-t null distribution; green outline is the vmPFC proxy. Small corrected foci occur posterior-inferior to the proxy and are not interpreted anatomically.\n    28\t\n    29\t![Whole-brain corrected map](results/wholebrain_fwe_map.png)\n    30\t\n    31\t## Reproducibility files\n    32\t\n    33\t- `analyze.py` — complete group-analysis and figure-generation script (Python with NumPy, pandas, SciPy, NiBabel, Nilearn, and Matplotlib).\n    34\t- `results/summary.json` — numeric analysis summary and QC decisions.\n    35\t- `results/fwe_clusters.tsv` — descriptive extents and peak coordinates for corrected voxels; cluster extent itself was not the inferential correction.\n    36\t- `results/participant_qc.tsv` — per-participant coverage and effect summaries.\n    37\t- `results/group_mask.nii.gz`, `results/mean_effect.nii.gz`, `results/t_statistic.nii.gz`, `results/p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz` — analysis mask, mean, t, and max-T adjusted p maps.\n    38\t- `results/vmPFC_proxy_aal3.nii.gz` — resampled anatomical proxy used for localization.\n    39\t\n    40\tReproduce from the workspace root with:\n    41\t\n    42\t```bash\n    43\t/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analyze.py\n    44\t```\n--- ANALYSIS LINE REFERENCES ---\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n     2\t\"\"\"Group analysis of supplied NARPS AO86 Hypothesis 1 participant cope maps.\"\"\"\n     3\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     4\timport json\n     5\timport hashlib\n     6\timport numpy as np\n     7\timport pandas as pd\n     8\timport nibabel as nib\n     9\tfrom nilearn import datasets, image, plotting\n    10\timport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    11\tfrom scipy import stats, ndimage\n    12\t\n    13\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    14\tOUT = ROOT / \"results\"\n    15\tOUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    16\tDATA = ROOT / \"input\" / \"data\"\n    17\tN_PERM = 5000\n    18\tSEED = 20261016\n    19\t\n    20\tfiles = sorted(DATA.glob(\"sub-*_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\"))\n    21\tassert len(files) == 54, f\"Expected 54 maps, found {len(files)}\"\n    22\tparticipants = pd.read_csv(ROOT / \"input\" / \"participants.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\")\n    23\texpected_ids = set(participants.loc[participants[\"group\"] == \"equalIndifference\", \"participant_id\"].astype(str))\n    24\tfound_ids = {p.name.split(\"_\")[0] for p in files}\n    25\tassert expected_ids == found_ids and len(expected_ids) == 54\n    26\tsource_manifest = json.loads((ROOT / \"input\" / \"sources.json\").read_text())\n    27\thash_checks = {p.name: hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == source_manifest[\"files\"][f\"data/{p.name}\"][\"sha256\"]\n    28\t               for p in files}\n    29\tassert len(hash_checks) == 54 and all(hash_checks.values()), \"Input checksum mismatch\"\n    30\timgs = [nib.load(str(p)) for p in files]\n    31\tref = imgs[0]\n    32\tassert all(im.shape == ref.shape and np.allclose(im.affine, ref.affine) for im in imgs)\n    33\tarr = np.stack([im.get_fdata(dtype=np.float32) for im in imgs])\n    34\tfinite = np.isfinite(arr)\n    35\tnonzero = finite & (arr != 0)\n    36\tcoverage = nonzero.sum(axis=0)\n    37\t# Intersect map coverage with an independent standard brain mask.\n    38\tstandard_mask = datasets.load_mni152_brain_mask(resolution=2, threshold=.2)\n    39\tstandard_mask_on_ref = image.resample_to_img(standard_mask, ref, interpolation=\"nearest\",\n    40\t                                              force_resample=True, copy_header=True)\n    41\tmask = ((coverage >= int(np.ceil(.90 * len(files)))) & np.all(finite, axis=0)\n    42\t        & (np.asarray(standard_mask_on_ref.dataobj) > 0))\n    43\tX = arr[:, mask].astype(np.float64)\n    44\tn, v = X.shape\n    45\tassert n == 54 and v > 10000\n    46\t\n    47\t# One-sample t statistic, positive direction. Random sign flips test the zero-mean null.\n    48\t# The same maximum statistic from every permutation controls whole-brain voxelwise FWER.\n    49\tsum_sq = np.sum(X * X, axis=0)\n    50\tdef t_from_sum(s):\n    51\t    denom2 = (n * sum_sq - s * s) / (n - 1)\n    52\t    return s / np.sqrt(np.maximum(denom2, np.finfo(float).tiny))\n    53\t\n    54\tt_obs = t_from_sum(X.sum(axis=0))\n    55\trng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n    56\tmax_t = np.empty(N_PERM, dtype=np.float64)\n    57\tbatch = 32\n    58\tfor start in range(0, N_PERM, batch):\n    59\t    b = min(batch, N_PERM - start)\n    60\t    signs = rng.choice(np.array([-1.0, 1.0]), size=(b, n))\n    61\t    sums = signs @ X\n    62\t    t_perm = sums / np.sqrt(np.maximum((n * sum_sq[None, :] - sums * sums) / (n - 1), np.finfo(float).tiny))\n    63\t    max_t[start:start+b] = np.max(t_perm, axis=1)\n    64\tsorted_max = np.sort(max_t)\n    65\t# plus-one Monte Carlo correction; adjusted p is based on whole-brain maximum T.\n    66\tidx = np.searchsorted(sorted_max, t_obs, side=\"left\")\n    67\tp_fwe = (N_PERM - idx + 1) / (N_PERM + 1)\n    68\t\n    69\tdef full_img(vals, dtype=np.float32):\n    70\t    a = np.zeros(ref.shape, dtype=dtype)\n    71\t    a[mask] = vals\n    72\t    return nib.Nifti1Image(a, ref.affine, ref.header)\n    73\t\n    74\tmean = X.mean(axis=0)\n    75\tsd = X.std(axis=0, ddof=1)\n    76\tnib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(mask.astype(np.uint8), ref.affine, ref.header), OUT / \"group_mask.nii.gz\")\n    77\tnib.save(full_img(mean), OUT / \"mean_effect.nii.gz\")\n    78\tnib.save(full_img(t_obs), OUT / \"t_statistic.nii.gz\")\n    79\tnib.save(full_img(p_fwe), OUT / \"p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz\")\n    80\t\n    81\t# Anatomical vmPFC proxy: bilateral medial orbitofrontal cortex from AAL3v2.\n    82\tatlas = datasets.fetch_atlas_aal(version=\"3v2\", data_dir=str(ROOT / \"atlas_cache\"), verbose=0)\n    83\tatlas_img = nib.load(atlas.maps) if isinstance(atlas.maps, str) else atlas.maps\n    84\tlabels = list(atlas.labels)\n    85\tlabel_text = [x.decode() if isinstance(x, bytes) else str(x) for x in labels]\n    86\troi_ids = [i for i, name in enumerate(label_text) if \"Frontal_Med_Orb\" in name]\n    87\tif not roi_ids:\n    88\t    raise RuntimeError(f\"AAL3 medial orbitofrontal labels not found: {label_text}\")\n    89\t# AAL uses background label 0; IDs align with label-table index.\n    90\tatlas_on_ref = image.resample_to_img(atlas_img, ref, interpolation=\"nearest\")\n    91\troi_native = np.isin(np.asarray(atlas_on_ref.dataobj), roi_ids)\n    92\troi = roi_native & mask\n    93\tif not roi.any():\n    94\t    raise RuntimeError(\"vmPFC proxy ROI has no overlap with group mask\")\n    95\troi_values = X[:, roi[mask]]\n    96\troi_mean = roi_values.mean(axis=1)\n    97\troi_sd = float(roi_mean.std(ddof=1))\n    98\troi_se = roi_sd / np.sqrt(n)\n    99\troi_t = float(roi_mean.mean() / roi_se)\n   100\troi_ci = [float(roi_mean.mean() - stats.t.ppf(.975, n-1) * roi_se),\n   101\t          float(roi_mean.mean() + stats.t.ppf(.975, n-1) * roi_se)]\n   102\troi_mask_img = nib.Nifti1Image(roi.astype(np.uint8), ref.affine, ref.header)\n   103\tnib.save(roi_mask_img, OUT / \"vmPFC_proxy_aal3.nii.gz\")\n   104\t\n   105\t# Summaries and QC, no data-driven subject exclusions.\n   106\tparticipant_mean = arr[:, mask].mean(axis=1)\n   107\tparticipant_sd = arr[:, mask].std(axis=1, ddof=1)\n   108\tparticipant_roi_mean = roi_values.mean(axis=1)\n   109\tqc = pd.DataFrame({\"participant\": [p.name.split(\"_\")[0] for p in files],\n   110\t                   \"mean_in_mask\": participant_mean, \"sd_in_mask\": participant_sd,\n   111\t                   \"mean_in_vmPFC_proxy\": participant_roi_mean,\n   112\t                   \"fraction_finite\": finite.reshape(n, -1).mean(axis=1),\n   113\t                   \"fraction_nonzero\": nonzero.reshape(n, -1).mean(axis=1)})\n   114\tqc.to_csv(OUT / \"participant_qc.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\", index=False)\n   115\t\n   116\tsumm = {\n   117\t    \"n_maps\": n, \"input_sha256_checks_passed\": bool(all(hash_checks.values())),\n   118\t    \"n_voxels_whole_brain_mask\": int(v), \"mask_rule\": \"MNI152 standard brain mask intersected with finite voxels nonzero in >=90% (>=49/54) maps\",\n   119\t    \"n_permutations\": N_PERM, \"seed\": SEED, \"test\": \"one-sided positive one-sample t with random sign flips and whole-brain maximum-T FWER\",\n   120\t    \"fwe_alpha\": 0.05, \"max_t_critical_95\": float(np.quantile(max_t, .95, method=\"higher\")),\n   121\t    \"whole_brain_sig_voxels\": int(np.sum(p_fwe <= .05)),\n   122\t    \"max_t_observed\": float(np.max(t_obs)), \"minimum_p_fwe\": float(np.min(p_fwe)),\n   123\t    \"group_mean_effect_range\": [float(mean.min()), float(mean.max())],\n   124\t    \"group_mean_effect_peak_mni\": [float(x) for x in nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, np.array(np.unravel_index(int(np.argmax(full_img(t_obs).get_fdata())), ref.shape)))],\n   125\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_atlas\": \"AAL3v2 bilateral Frontal_Med_Orb\", \"vmPFC_label_ids\": roi_ids,\n   126\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_voxels\": int(roi.sum()), \"vmPFC_proxy_mean_effect\": float(roi_mean.mean()),\n   127\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_sd_between_participants\": roi_sd,\n   128\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_mean_effect_95CI_t_descriptive\": roi_ci,\n   129\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_mean_t_descriptive\": roi_t,\n   130\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_p_positive_t_descriptive\": float(stats.t.sf(roi_t, n-1)),\n   131\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_min_whole_brain_adjusted_p\": float(p_fwe[roi[mask]].min()),\n   132\t    \"vmPFC_proxy_significant_voxels_fwe05\": int(np.sum(p_fwe[roi[mask]] <= .05)),\n   133\t    \"participant_mean_effect_mean\": float(participant_mean.mean()),\n   134\t    \"participant_mean_effect_sd\": float(participant_mean.std(ddof=1)),\n   135\t    \"exclusions\": [],\n   136\t}\n   137\t(OUT / \"summary.json\").write_text(json.dumps(summ, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n   138\t\n   139\t# Connected components are descriptive summaries of the globally corrected voxels.\n   140\tsig_data = np.zeros(ref.shape, dtype=bool)\n   141\tsig_data[mask] = p_fwe <= .05\n   142\tcomponents, n_comp = ndimage.label(sig_data, structure=ndimage.generate_binary_structure(3, 3))\n   143\tt_full = np.zeros(ref.shape, dtype=np.float64)\n   144\tt_full[mask] = t_obs\n   145\tcluster_rows = []\n   146\tfor lab in range(1, n_comp + 1):\n   147\t    ijk = np.argwhere(components == lab)\n   148\t    tvals = t_full[tuple(ijk.T)]\n   149\t    peak_ijk = ijk[int(np.argmax(tvals))]\n   150\t    xyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, peak_ijk)\n   151\t    cluster_rows.append({\"cluster\": lab, \"voxels_input_grid\": len(ijk), \"peak_t\": float(tvals.max()),\n   152\t                         \"peak_mni_x\": float(xyz[0]), \"peak_mni_y\": float(xyz[1]), \"peak_mni_z\": float(xyz[2])})\n   153\tpd.DataFrame(cluster_rows).to_csv(OUT / \"fwe_clusters.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\", index=False)\n   154\t\n   155\t# Participant vmPFC proxy averages: one value per participant, with a descriptive t interval.\n   156\tplt.rcParams.update({\"font.size\": 9, \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False})\n   157\tfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.8, 4.2), constrained_layout=True)\n   158\tax.scatter(np.random.default_rng(SEED).normal(0, .045, n), roi_mean, s=24, alpha=.75,\n   159\t           color=\"#547a9a\", edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=.3)\n   160\tax.errorbar(0, roi_mean.mean(), yerr=[[roi_mean.mean()-roi_ci[0]], [roi_ci[1]-roi_mean.mean()]],\n   161\t            fmt=\"D\", color=\"#b54b3a\", capsize=4, markersize=7, label=\"Mean and 95% t CI\")\n   162\tax.axhline(0, color=\"black\", linewidth=1, linestyle=\"--\")\n   163\tax.set(xlim=(-.25,.25), xlabel=\"Participants (jittered)\", ylabel=\"Mean effect in vmPFC proxy (supplied units)\",\n   164\t       title=\"Bilateral medial orbitofrontal proxy\")\n   165\tax.set_xticks([])\n   166\tax.legend(frameon=False, fontsize=8)\n   167\tfig.savefig(OUT / \"vmPFC_proxy_effects.png\", dpi=180)\n   168\tplt.close(fig)\n   169\t\n   170\t# Whole-brain corrected positive group findings; green outline shows the independent ROI proxy.\n   171\tfig = plt.figure(figsize=(7.0, 5.0))\n   172\ttemplate = datasets.load_mni152_template(resolution=2)\n   173\tdisplay = plotting.plot_stat_map(full_img(t_obs), bg_img=template, threshold=float(np.quantile(max_t, .95, method=\"higher\")),\n   174\t                                 display_mode=\"ortho\", cut_coords=(-26, -102, -4), cmap=\"hot\", colorbar=True,\n   175\t                                 black_bg=False, figure=fig, title=None, draw_cross=True)\n   176\tdisplay.add_contours(roi_mask_img, levels=[.5], colors=[\"#18a558\"], linewidths=1.5)\n   177\tfig.suptitle(\"Positive t above whole-brain max-T FWE threshold\\nGreen: bilateral vmPFC proxy\", fontsize=12)\n   178\tfig.savefig(OUT / \"wholebrain_fwe_map.png\", dpi=180)\n   179\tplt.close(fig)\n   180\t\n   181\tprint(json.dumps(summ, indent=2))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat >\"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/build-records.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport os, json, hashlib, pathlib\nout=pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\nmanifest_path=pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST'])\nmanifest=json.loads(manifest_path.read_text())\ncap_sha=hashlib.sha256(manifest_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\nfiles={}\nfor row in manifest['entries']:\n    p=row['path']\n    if p.startswith('content/workspace/'):\n        files[p[len('content/workspace/'):]]=row\n\ndef ev(path, desc):\n    row=files.get(path,{})\n    return {'uri':path,'description':desc,'sha256':row.get('sha256')}\ndef probe(desc):\n    p=out/'probes.json'\n    return {'uri':str(p),'description':desc,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\nitems={\n'must/001':('unmet','The delivered command depends on a user-specific interpreter outside the common root.','judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Reproduction command uses an absolute interpreter path outside the project (line 43).')]),\n'must/002':('met','All 54 required effect maps and cohort metadata are supplied under input and connected to the analysis.','judgement',[],[ev('analyze.py','Analysis enumerates and checks all 54 input maps against participant metadata and the source manifest (lines 20–29).'),ev('input/sources.json','Identifies all 54 source maps and metadata.')]),\n'must/003':('unmet','Python packages are named, but no environment file includes or installs them.','judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Lists package names but provides no environment specification (lines 31–43).'),ev('analyze.py','Imports the analysis dependencies (lines 6–11).')]),\n'must/004':('partial','Git tracks supplied inputs, but the worker analysis, report and generated results remained uncommitted at stop.','probe:tree-clean+judgement',['mapping-questioned'],[probe('Probe found four untracked worker deliverables in the complete stop state.'),ev('.git/HEAD','Worker HEAD at stop.'),ev('analyze.py','Delivered analysis script is outside the committed state.')]),\n'must/005':('met','git-annex pointers and local annex content preserve the large participant maps.','probe:large-in-annex+judgement',['mapping-questioned'],[ev('.git/config','Repository activates the git-annex filter.'),ev('.git/annex','Captured local git-annex metadata and content tree.'),probe('Probe recognized 54 annex pointers; its .datalad/config citation is a heuristic path mismatch.')]),\n'must/006':('unmet','The shipped results have no run record linking their generation to a captured exact environment.','probe:run-env-linked+judgement',[],[ev('results/summary.json','Results report method and numeric summaries but no environment identity or action record.'),ev('REPORT.md','Only reproduction instruction points to an external interpreter (line 43).'),probe('Probe found no environment-linked run record.')]),\n'must/007':('unmet','The report gives a run command but no installation instructions or usable environment setup.','probe:entry-point+judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Reproduction section names an external Python executable but gives no installation route (lines 31–43).')]),\n'must/008':('met','The complete stop includes analyze.py and the report names it as the reproduction entrypoint.','probe:entry-point+judgement',['probe-overridden'],[ev('REPORT.md','Names analyze.py and gives the launch command (lines 31–43).'),ev('analyze.py','Complete group-analysis entrypoint is present in the stopped workspace.'),probe('Probe missed untracked files and reported no entrypoint from tracked paths.')]),\n'must/009':('unmet','The documented reproduction command contains a host-specific absolute path.','probe:no-abs-paths+judgement',['probe-overridden'],[ev('REPORT.md','Absolute /Users/.../common-environment interpreter path (line 43).'),probe('Probe scanned tracked text only; it did not inspect untracked REPORT.md.')]),\n'must/010':('unmet','No complete dependency specification declares package versions or the Python runtime.','probe:env-spec-tracked+judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Names packages but contains no lockfile or environment specification (lines 31–43).'),ev('analyze.py','Imports NumPy, pandas, NiBabel, Nilearn, Matplotlib and SciPy (lines 6–11).')]),\n'must/011':('unmet','The external interpreter path is host-specific, while OS/runtime assumptions are undocumented.','probe:platform-assumptions+judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Uses a user-home interpreter path without documenting its host requirements (line 43).'),probe('Command scan found no platform-specific utilities; documentation still has an unresolved host assumption.')]),\n'must/012':('unmet','Package names appear in prose, but system/runtime requirements and installation dependencies are not specified.','probe:platform-assumptions+judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Dependency names and incomplete run instructions (lines 31–43).')]),\n'must/013':('unmet','No environment specification is tracked with the committed project state.','probe:env-spec-tracked+judgement',[],[ev('.git/HEAD','Captured worker commit identifies the committed state.'),ev('REPORT.md','Lists dependencies without a checked-in specification (lines 31–43).'),probe('No tracked environment specification found.')]),\n'must/014':('unmet','No command or process for updating environment specifications is provided.','probe:env-spec-tracked+judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Reproduction section has no environment update process (lines 31–43).')]),\n'must/015':('unmet','No frozen package manifest or exact environment identity accompanies the results.','probe:run-env-linked+judgement',[],[ev('results/summary.json','Numerical result record omits environment identity.'),ev('REPORT.md','Uses an external interpreter path with no version/lock (line 43).')]),\n'must/016':('unmet','No environment specification is present to share; the documented interpreter is outside the captured project.','probe:env-spec-tracked+judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','External interpreter path is not an archived environment (line 43).'),probe('No tracked environment specification or publication route found.')]),\n'must/017':('unmet','Users are not told how to obtain or reconstruct the external environment.','judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Reproduction command assumes a user-specific interpreter path (lines 40–43).')]),\n'should/001':('partial','Git and git-annex cover supplied inputs, but the analysis code and results are uncommitted.','probe:tree-clean+judgement',['mapping-questioned'],[ev('.git/config','One Git repository with git-annex configured.'),ev('analyze.py','Analysis code is untracked at worker stop.'),probe('Probe records the untracked deliverables.')]),\n'should/002':('not-checked','The delivery has no regular-testing record; worker-authored repeated-run evidence would settle this.','judgement',[],[probe('No recognized CI file; this does not rule out equivalent repeated testing.')]),\n'should/003':('partial','Inputs, code and results occupy separate directories, but no environment module is provided.','probe:modules-separated+judgement',[],[ev('analyze.py','Code reads under input/ and writes under results/.'),ev('REPORT.md','Names input, code and result artifacts (lines 31–38).'),probe('Recognized input separation only.')]),\n'should/004':('not-checked','No fresh-environment run is recorded; replay was unsafe because its only interpreter is outside the captured delivery.','judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Documented interpreter prerequisite (line 43).'),{'uri':'replay-record.json','description':'Assessment replay decision: not checked; no execution attempted.','sha256':None}]),\n'should/005':('unmet','The documented command reuses a fixed user-level Pixi environment rather than creating a disposable one.','judgement',[],[ev('REPORT.md','Points to a persistent common-environment path (line 43).')]),\n'should/006':('unmet','There is no environment specification whose re