{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/write-report.py\" | sed -n '\"'1,22p;88,115p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\timport os, json, pathlib, hashlib\n     2\tout=pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\n     3\tresp=json.loads((out/'2026-10-16-response.json').read_text())\n     4\tmanifest=json.loads(pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']).read_text())\n     5\tcap_sha=hashlib.sha256(pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n     6\treport='''# Independent assessment — NARPS Hypothesis 1\n     7\t\n     8\tAssessment date: 2026-10-16 (UTC). This report assesses the complete worker-stop capture, including uncommitted and ignored files. Citations to target artifacts below use capture-relative paths within `content/workspace`; their identity is canonical capture SHA-256 `CAPTURE_SHA`.\n     9\t\n    10\t## STAMPED verdicts\n    11\t\n    12\tMUST: 3 met / 1 partial / 13 unmet / 0 not-checked (17 total). SHOULD: 1 met / 1 partial / 4 unmet / 3 not-checked (9 total). MAY: 1 met / 1 partial / 3 unmet / 0 not-checked (5 total). No overall score is assigned.\n    13\t\n    14\t## Scientific assessment\n    15\t\n    16\t**Scientific adequacy: qualified.** The delivered analysis supports its reported conclusion that these supplied maps do not establish a positive vmPFC association under whole-brain FWE correction. The result is conditional on the supplied participant estimates and has important spatial and uncertainty limits described below.\n    17\t\n    18\tHypothesis conclusion (verbatim): In the 54-person NARPS equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not** support a positive gain association in vmPFC under whole-brain family-wise error (FWE) correction.\n    19\t\n    20\tThe worker used 54 independent participant gain-effect maps and an unweighted one-sample t model, appropriate to the supplied contrast estimates and the absence of participant variance maps. `analyze.py` verifies the cohort IDs, per-image source hashes, common shape and affine; it excludes no participant. The mask requires at least 49/54 nonzero maps, finite values in every map, and overlap with a standard brain mask. The code uses 5,000 seeded sign flips and the maximum positive t over 192,339 voxels for one-sided whole-brain FWE inference. This directly addresses the required correction and does not substitute an uncorrected ROI test. The report identifies bilateral AAL3v2 `Frontal_Med_Orb` as an explicit anatomical proxy for vmPFC and keeps the ROI summary descriptive.\n    21\t\n    22\tThe delivered `results/summary.json` reports a proxy mean of −0.00795 supplied units, descriptive 95% t interval [−0.03455, 0.01864], zero proxy voxels surviving whole-brain correction, and 23 corrected voxels in three posterior-inferior foci. The report does not treat those foci as vmPFC evidence. It correctly states that these are not effects per currency unit because the upstream gain regressor was variance-normalized, that the result depends on the fixed separate gain/loss first-level model, and that absence of corrected support is not proof of zero or absence of any neural correlate.\n    88\tChecklist link: [open the filled STAMPED checklist](2026-10-16-url.txt). Full item responses and evidence hashes: [2026-10-16-response.json](2026-10-16-response.json). Raw probe output: [2026-10-16-probes.json](2026-10-16-probes.json). Replay decision: [replay-record.json](replay-record.json). Access check: [access-record.json](access-record.json).\n    89\t\n    90\tProduced by `assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles` 0.1.0 with `stamped-conventions` 0.1.0, checklist 0.3.1 (`stamped-checklist-schema@v0.3.1`, `af259ba`), on canonical capture `CAPTURE_SHA`, 2026-10-16, Codex / GPT-6. Probe output: `2026-10-16-probes.json`. The frozen assessment runtime was used for probe, response and validation actions.\n    91\t'''\n    92\t# Insert values and the pinned item table.\n    93\ttable=(out/'2026-10-16-item-table.md').read_text()\n    94\treport=report.replace('CAPTURE_SHA',cap_sha).replace('REPORT_SHA',filesha('REPORT.md')).replace('ANALYZE_SHA',filesha('analyze.py')).replace('SUMMARY_SHA',filesha('results/summary.json')).replace('CLUSTERS_SHA',filesha('results/fwe_clusters.tsv')).replace('QC_SHA',filesha('results/participant_qc.tsv')).replace('ITEM_TABLE',table)\n    95\tpath=out/'2026-10-16-assessment.md'; path.write_text(report)\n    96\t# The excerpts are anchored to physical report lines.\n    97\tlines=report.splitlines()\n    98\tadequacy_line=next(i for i,s in enumerate(lines,1) if s=='**Scientific adequacy: qualified.** The delivered analysis supports its reported conclusion that these supplied maps do not establish a positive vmPFC association under whole-brain FWE correction. The result is conditional on the supplied participant estimates and has important spatial and uncertainty limits described below.')\n    99\thyp_line=next(i for i,s in enumerate(lines,1) if s.startswith('Hypothesis conclusion (verbatim): '))\n   100\thyp_quote=lines[hyp_line-1].split('Hypothesis conclusion (verbatim): ',1)[1]\n   101\t# Retain the verbatim content with its Markdown emphasis.\n   102\trecord={'schema_version':1,'delivery_capture_sha256':cap_sha,'scientific_adequacy':'qualified','report':{'path':'2026-10-16-assessment.md','sha256':hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},'adequacy_evidence':{'quote':'Scientific adequacy: qualified.','start_line':adequacy_line,'end_line':adequacy_line},'hypothesis_conclusion':{'quote':hyp_quote,'start_line':hyp_line,'end_line':hyp_line}}\n   103\t(out/'scientific-judgment.json').write_text(json.dumps(record,indent=2)+'\\n')\n   104\t# Bind response assessor fields not filled by the helper's capture stamp.\n   105\trpath=out/'2026-10-16-response.json'; r=json.loads(rpath.read_text()); r['assessor'].update({'skill':'assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles','version':'0.1.0','date':'2026-10-16'}); rpath.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\n')\n   106\t# Copy raw probe receipt to the date-stamped required product.\n   107\t(out/'2026-10-16-probes.json').write_bytes((out/'probes.json').read_bytes())\n   108\t# Correctly classify newly created annex SQLite side files only if they are regular files.\n   109\taudit=json.loads((out/'integrity-audit.json').read_text())\n   110\tfor m in list(audit.get('integrity_invalidating_mismatches',[])):\n   111\t    rel=m['path']\n   112\t    if rel in ('.git/annex/keysdb/db-shm','.git/annex/keysdb/db-wal'):\n   113\t        st=(pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET'])/rel).lstat()\n   114\t        if pathlib.stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):\n   115\t            audit['integrity_invalidating_mismatches'].remove(m); audit.setdefault('operational_metadata_mismatches',[]).append(m)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
